  "doctrine": {
    "summary": "Korean People's Army Ground Force: a very large conscript army (service of up to 10 years) with heavily fortified positions along the DMZ, massed artillery and rocket forces, extensive tunnels and underground facilities, and very large light-infantry and special-operations forces. From late 2024 roughly 11,000-15,000 KPA troops were deployed to Russia's Kursk region to fight Ukraine, where they suffered heavy losses but adapted quickly to drone warfare; Pyongyang supplied shells, KN-23 missiles, Koksan guns and 240 mm rocket launchers to Russia.",
    "squad_size": 10,
    "fireteam": "Rifle squad of 9-10 with a squad machine gun and RPG; light-infantry and sniper brigades operate in small teams. Game: 8 in four pairs.",
    "tactics": [
      "Dense human-wave-style dismounted assaults across open ground (observed in Kursk), accepting high losses",
      "Hardened bunker and tunnel networks along the DMZ (map hazard and spawn points)",
      "Massed tube and rocket artillery preparation (Koksan, 240 mm, KN-25 off-map)",
      "Special-operations and light-infantry infiltration behind lines in small teams",
      "Rapid learning of counter-drone tactics: shooting at drones, spreading out, using decoy soldiers",
      "Strong political discipline: units rarely surrender"
    ],
